{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/y90nupkv","slideIndex":0,"text":"Compass CSR Chat. Full October 2026 month in review.\n\nSources: compass-csr-chat-queries-2026-04.xlsx through compass-csr-chat-queries-2026-10.xlsx in Minerva/_Data/Monthly-Extracts. Monthly files are authoritative. The all-time workbook ends August 24 Pacific and adds no timestamp/user keys beyond the monthly sources.\n\nPacific date boundaries, October 1 through October 31 inclusive. User IDs trimmed and case-normalized. Excluded IDs matching test|smoke|demo|admin|service|svc plus unique_user_identifier. Historical baselines are consistently recalculated, which revises the previous September slide from 1,336 to 1,335 MAU and August from 1,292 to 1,290.\n\nOctober: 1672 MAU; 37741 queries; 1062 retained, 534 first-observed, 76 reacquired and 273 lapsed. Retention is 1062/1335. New means first observed since April 7; reacquired means active before September, absent in September, active in October. Lapsed means active in September and no October queries. These are activity classifications, not account cancellations or verified signups.\n\nDAU P50 and weekday query average use 22 Monday-Friday dates in each month. Saturdays and Sundays are omitted from these daily statistics. October Saturday queries: 558, Sunday: 0. October weekday DAU P50: 520.5, P95: 583.8, mean: 511.27. October weekday query mean: 1690.14.\n\nWAU chart: number of distinct users with a query in each trailing seven-calendar-day window, evaluated at each weekday endpoint. P50 July 691, August 893, September 912.5, October 1042.5. P95 September 963.9, October 1132.75. Windows may cross month boundaries and use observed historical activity. Overlapping windows are descriptive, not independent samples. Displayed counts round halves upward; growth uses unrounded values.\n\nOctober retained users produced 32,576 queries versus 29,566 for the same users in September, an increase of 10.18%. Overall queries per MAU fell from 24.05 to 22.57 with the larger new-user cohort. No causal attribution is inferred.\n\nOctober reacquired users: 76, 552 queries, median 3 queries and 2 active days. Forty-four (57.9%) returned on a later date; 35 (46.1%) in a later calendar week. Median complete inactive gap before return: 61 days, range 30-191. Of the September 48 reacquired users, 28 (58.3%) were active in October.\n\nAnswer times measure logged response latency only. Query records do not establish answer correctness or end-to-end service reliability. Detailed definitions, observations, limitations and recommendations are in the accompanying summary.\n\nNovember 16 correction: two charts cover August, September and October 2026. MAU columns pair with monthly query totals. WAU P50 columns pair with P50 weekly query counts. Each series is independently indexed to its own August baseline, set to 100. Labels display actual counts, not index values.\n\nMonthly active users: 1290, 1335, 1672. Monthly WAU P50: 893, 912.5, 1042.5. Monthly queries in the MAU chart: 29482, 32113, 37741. P50 weekly queries in the WAU chart: 6915, 7678, 8503.5. Each index equals the current value divided by its August value, times 100.\n\nThe WAU measure is the monthly median of rolling seven-calendar-day active-user counts, evaluated at weekday endpoints. For weekly query P50, count every query in each of those identical windows, then take the monthly median. Windows include the endpoint and the preceding six calendar dates, can cross month boundaries, and retain observed Saturday/Sunday queries. August, September and October contain 21, 22 and 22 weekday endpoints. No extrapolation or division of monthly totals is used.\n\nExact WAU values are 893, 912.5 and 1042.5. WAU labels round half upwards to 893, 913 and 1,043. Weekly query medians are 6,915, 7,678 and 8,503.5 and retain fractional precision in labels. Growth uses unrounded values.\n\nOctober MoM growth: MAU 25.2434%, WAU P50 14.2466%, monthly queries 17.5256%, P50 weekly queries 10.7515%. The active-user changes appear as +25.2% and +14.2% in green header badges matching the +337 NET styling. Query-growth figures appear below their respective charts. The previous report and source slide remain preserved."}